From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: print a leftover crash
 reason at probe

Not for source= beyond the investigation it belongs to.

The remote processor writes a reason string into its SMEM crash item
before it goes down, and qcom_q6v5 reads that item from the fatal and
watchdog interrupt handlers. On this board the SoC resets hard enough
that neither handler ever runs -- no "fatal error received", no "watchdog
received", nothing -- so the string, if there is one, is never read.

SMEM lives in DDR and survives a reset well enough that ramoops works
across one, so a reason written just before the modem died should still
be there on the way back up. Read it at probe and say so either way.

The reset this is for happens seconds after the modem registers on the
network, with IPA loaded, and has so far produced no CPU exception, no
SMMU fault, no IPA or GSI error once those are unmasked, no watchdog
bark, and nothing in the firmware regions the vendor reserves for a
dump. The modem's own account of it is the last thing left to ask for.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -254,6 +254,30 @@
 	q6v5->rproc = rproc;
 	q6v5->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	q6v5->crash_reason = crash_reason;
+
+	/*
+	 * DIAGNOSTIC: report whatever is already in the crash reason item.
+	 *
+	 * The remote writes this string to SMEM before it dies, and this
+	 * driver only ever reads it from the fatal and watchdog interrupt
+	 * handlers. On this board the SoC resets so abruptly that neither
+	 * handler runs, so nobody looks. SMEM is in DDR and survives a reset
+	 * well enough for ramoops to work, so if the modem managed to write a
+	 * reason before going down it should still be here on the way back up.
+	 */
+	if (crash_reason) {
+		size_t len;
+		char *msg;
+
+		msg = qcom_smem_get(QCOM_SMEM_HOST_ANY, crash_reason, &len);
+		if (!IS_ERR(msg) && len > 0 && msg[0])
+			dev_err(&pdev->dev,
+				"crash reason left in SMEM item %d: %s\n",
+				crash_reason, msg);
+		else
+			dev_info(&pdev->dev,
+				 "SMEM item %d empty at probe\n", crash_reason);
+	}
 	q6v5->handover = handover;
 
 	init_completion(&q6v5->start_done);
